rgin:0 0 16px;">For years she has been in and out of contact with it, and it has been a struggle. Now she has an easy way to hear her body speak to her, one she can come back to and whose wisdom she can rely on. That was the relief in her tears.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">I&rsquo;m giving a retreat right now. In moments like this, talking with the people here, I&rsquo;m reminded how truly simple and how powerful somatic sounding is.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">You don&rsquo;t need a retreat to begin. The workshop is seventy minutes, live on Zoom. You ask a question your mind can&rsquo;t answer first, you breathe in, and you let your body make one tone: the tone of what&rsquo;s there, right now. That is where the listening starts.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 0px;">If you have never made a sound with us, come and listen to your own body. Through Monday 30&nbsp;November a seat is half price.</p></td></tr>
