<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background-color:#EADFCB;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;">
<span class="preheader">What a woman told me at the retreat I’m giving. The 12-week course and the certification path, half price through Monday.&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;</span>
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="background-color:#EADFCB;">
<tr><td align="center" style="padding:24px 12px;">
<table role="presentation" class="wrapper" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width:600px;background-color:#F4ECDF;border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden;">
<tr><td align="center" style="background-color:#2A1B2A;padding:11px 20px;text-align:center;"><p style="margin:0;font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:2px;color:#F4ECDF;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;">Black Friday &middot; through Monday 30&nbsp;November</p></td></tr>
<tr><td class="pad" style="padding:38px 44px 6px;"><table role="presentation" dir="rtl" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td dir="ltr" class="seal-td" width="160" valign="top" align="right" style="width:160px;padding:0;vertical-align:top;text-align:right;"><a href="https://songdance.co/courses/12-week?utm_source=broadcast&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=bfcm_2026&amp;utm_content=b-workshop2_hero&amp;{{prefill}}#register" style="display:block;"><img class="seal-img" src="https://songdance.co/email/bfcm/seal-courses.png" width="160" alt="50% off both courses" style="width:160px;height:auto;font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.4;color:#A14826;"></a></td><td dir="ltr" class="hd-td" valign="top" align="left" style="padding:0 14px 0 0;vertical-align:top;text-align:left;"><p class="eye" style="margin:0 0 22px;font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:2.5px;color:#A14826;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;"><span style="display:inline-block;width:26px;height:1px;background-color:#A14826;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:12px;"></span>The 12-week course &amp; the certification path</p><h1 class="h1b" style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:38px;line-height:1.14;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 28px;">Today at lunch, <br><em style="font-family:''Cormorant Garamond'',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:500;font-size:1.05em;color:#C9603A;">tears of joy.</em></h1></td></tr></table><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">Hello {{ subscriber.first_name | default: "there" }},</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">Today at lunch a woman told me, in tears of joy, how surprised and relieved she is. She can finally listen to her body.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">For years she has been in and out of contact with it, and it has been a struggle. Now she has an easy way to hear her body speak to her, one she can come back to and whose wisdom she can rely on. That was the relief in her tears.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">I&rsquo;m giving a retreat right now. In moments like this, talking with the people here, I&rsquo;m reminded how truly simple and how powerful somatic sounding is.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">You have sounded with us, in a workshop or a masterclass, so you know the first taste of this. What she was describing is what it is like once it is yours: a way of listening you can come back to on an ordinary day, at home.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 0px;">That takes more than one hour. It takes a while, and a map. That is the 12-week course, and through Monday 30&nbsp;November it is half price. So is the certification path, for those who want to hold space for others.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td class="pad" style="padding:34px 44px 6px;"><h2 class="offer-h" style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:27px;line-height:1.22;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 18px;">For yourself, <em style="font-family:''Cormorant Garamond'',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:500;font-size:1.05em;color:#C9603A;">or for others too?</em></h2><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;"><strong style="font-weight:600;">If you want this for yourself:</strong> the 12-week course. A practice that fits in a kitchen. Twelve modules, a live hour with me every week from the day you join, and the materials stay yours for life.</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 0px;"><strong style="font-weight:600;">If people already come to you with what they carry:</strong> the certification path. First the same 12 weeks, because nobody holds space for a sound they haven&rsquo;t made themselves. Then nine months of learning to hold that space. A space holder, not a healer: the person in front of you heals themselves. And you get to be there when someone finds what she found.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td class="pad" style="padding:34px 44px 6px;"><h2 class="offer-h" style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:27px;line-height:1.22;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 18px;">Twelve modules, <em style="font-family:''Cormorant Garamond'',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:500;font-size:1.05em;color:#C9603A;">one practice</em></h2><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">What the 12-week course walks through, at your own pace, with a live Q&amp;A every week to bring your questions to:</p><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-bottom:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">1 &middot; Understanding vocal sound</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Singing, toning, chanting, sounding, and why this practice is its own thing.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">2 &middot; Becoming comfortable</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Meeting the collective unease around using the voice.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">3 &middot; Holding space</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Steady, grounded footing for sound work, for yourself and others.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">4 &middot; Reading your sound</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Hearing the feeling and the pattern inside the voice.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">5 &middot; Neuroanatomy</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">The brain, the body and the voice, in plain terms.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">6 &middot; Nervous system flow</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Using sound to regulate and settle.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">7 &middot; The five core wounds</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Rejection, abandonment, betrayal, humiliation, injustice. Met at your own pace, through sound.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">8 &middot; Sounding toward essence</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">A meditation that listens toward your own essential sound.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">9 &middot; Sounds of the chakras</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">The energy centres, explored through tone.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">10 &middot; Sounding with instruments</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Voice with drum, shruti, or singing bowl.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">11 &middot; Practising with others</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">First steps in sounding together.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">12 &middot; Self-healing &amp; integration</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Carrying the practice forward on your own.</p></td></tr></table></td></tr>
<tr><td class="pad" style="padding:34px 44px 6px;"><h2 class="offer-h" style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:27px;line-height:1.22;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 18px;">And in the nine months <em style="font-family:''Cormorant Garamond'',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:500;font-size:1.05em;color:#C9603A;">after</em></h2><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 16px;">The certification path adds the training in holding space for someone else. There you learn:</p><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-bottom:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">To travel through the layers of a sound</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">How to recognise feelings in a voice (high, low, trembling, sharp), how to follow what is underneath the first sound, and how to guide a whole session from beginning to end.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">The emotions underneath</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Anger, fear, pain and grief. How each one moves, how it disguises itself, and how to meet it through the voice.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">Listening with the body</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Telling grief from pain, fear from overwhelm. Hearing what the voice is almost saying.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:14px 0 15px;border-top:1px solid #E2D5C1;"><p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;color:#2A1B2A;margin:0 0 5px;">Skills for holding the space</p><p style="font-family:Figtree,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;color:#4A3848;margin:0;">Pacing. Regulation. The volume button. Knowing when to lead, when to hold, and when to let the silence do the work.</p></td></tr></table></td></tr>
